===========================================
     Memories Configurability  
     Multi Processor Designs
===========================================

The following features can be configured for the ARM946ES DSM : 

	1- The device identifier, for multi processor designs. 
	   Up to 8 ARM946ES DSMs can run concurrently in a single design

	2- The sizes of the memories :
              * ICACHE and DCACHE - Default values : 8 Kbytes
          Maximum size : 1 Mb  

	


To configure the DSM, the user must modify the component instanciation 
of the ARM946ES, by adding the lines of the required generic(s) Verilog 
'defparam' mappings.

For example, to configure the 5 th processor of the design with 16 Kb of ICache and 32Kb of DCache, the user will 
add the following mappings : 


     If the ARM946ES model is instantiated as theARM946ES add the following :

           defparam theARM946ES.ID              = 5     ; 
           defparam theARM946ES.ICACHE_SIZE     = 16384 ;     // size in bytes
           defparam theARM946ES.DCACHE_SIZE     = 32768 ;     // size in bytes

           // COMPONENT INSTANCIATION
           ARM946ES theARM946ES (HADDR, ... etc ... )





             NOTE THAT : 
    ===============================

1- To set one generic parameter, and let the others to their default values, the user 
   just needs to add the line of this particular parameter, and not to bother about 
   the others. 

2- Default values : 
   - ICACHE and DCACHE sizes : 8 Kbytes
   - the device identifier is 0

3- The sizes of the memories must be integers, powers of 2, and be given in bytes.

4- The 'model identifier' (generic/defparam 'ID') is an integer from 0 to 7.
   This identifier allows the software to distinguish different instanciations
   of the same model in a single design. 

===========================================
            EIS Tracing
===========================================

This model supports the use of multiple 'log.eis' EIS trace files. 
The log file written to is controlled by means of the generic/defparam 'ID'.

For example if 'ID' is 3, the output is written to 'log.eis3'
By default 'ID' is '0' and the output goes to 'log.eis'

To set the value of 'ID', follow the instructions given at the previous 
paragraph :  'Memories Configurability  
              Multi Processor Designs'


The EIS trace enable is comtrolled via the environment variable :

eis_dont_generate

To turn off eis tracing set eis_dont_generate be non zero
eg setenv eis_dont_generate 1      

- this  will turn off eis tracing 
- if not set, outputs  to log.eis ( or log.eis<ID> )  as usual


It has echo to stdout capability controlled by environment variable:

 eis_echo_to_stdout

To turn on echo to stdout set the environment variable to be non zero

if not set ,only logs to file.


Summary of EIS tracing
======================

Default EIS tracing is :

EIS tracing ON 

EIS is logged in file called "log.eis", or "log.eis<ID>" ( ID  1 ... 7 ) 
in case of multiple ARM946Es instanciations in the design.

NO echo to screen .

To turn OFF the  EIS tracing set environment variable "eis_dont_generate"

To turn ON echo to stdout  set environment variable "eis_echo_to_stdout"



